 "narration": "A biological drawing is a scientific record. It must show what you can actually see, accurately and clearly. Use a sharp pencil and draw clear, continuous single lines. Do not shade or colour. Draw only a few representative cells, not the whole field of view, and show their true shapes. Draw label lines with a ruler, and the lines must not cross, and each must touch the part it labels. Give the drawing a title that names the specimen, and state the magnification used, for example Onion epidermal cells, ×100. Draw only the features you can actually see. Remember that onion cells have a cell wall and cheek cells do not. A drawing needs a title, a stated magnification and ruled, non-crossing label lines.",
 "narration_sentences": [
  "A biological drawing is a scientific record.",
